<title>SINGAPORE: Indonesia allocates 282,000 bpd Nov crude exports.</title>
<headline>Indonesia allocates 282,000 bpd Nov crude exports.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indonesia has cut crude export allocations in November to 282,000 barrels per day (bpd) from a month-earlier 345,000 bpd, industry sources said on Thursday.</p>
<p>State-owned Pertamina allocated 71,000 bpd of Minas, compared with just under 70,000 bpd in October.</p>
<p>Other major crude allocations were Widuri at 18,000 bpd from 29,000 bpd in October, Cinta at 19,000 bpd from 24,000 bpd, Belida at 12,000 from 13,000 and Duri at 80,000, which was steady from October.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65 870 3081)</p>
